Semiconductor manufacturing encompasses the processes used to produce integrated circuits and other semiconductor devices from silicon wafers. These processes include photolithography, deposition, etching, doping, wafer inspection, and testing. The resulting components power smartphones, computers, vehicles, industrial equipment, telecommunications networks, and data centers.

The industry is becoming increasingly capital-intensive as manufacturers pursue smaller process nodes, improved transistor architectures, and more sophisticated packaging technologies. At the same time, mature-node manufacturing remains important for automotive electronics, industrial control systems, power management, and connected devices.

Asia-Pacific leads the global semiconductor manufacturing market, supported by an established ecosystem of foundries, integrated device manufacturers, equipment suppliers, and semiconductor packaging companies.

